      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T21:24:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This textureView actually contradicts with the [6. new texture view base array layer restriction in compat mode](https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/compatibility-mode.md#6-array-texture-views-used-in-bind-groups-must-consist-of-the-entire-array-that-is-basearraylayer-must-be-zero-and-arraylayercount-must-be-equal-to-the-size-of-the-texture-array)\n\nBut `dstView` is used as render target and the arrayLayer essentially is passed to `gl.FramebufferTextureLayer` which is valid. [code](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/opengl/TextureGL.cpp;l\u003d615;drc\u003d5da3e004cb817f22367e498c16e317b9b6c0e62a)\n\nWe may need to mark this as internal to still make it work, if we implement the new compat validation rule",
      "revId": "e1922a21f12283a41150c7cff3ab305c816ea113",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe204a09_93b0ba54",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BlitBufferToDepthStencil.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 444,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T21:36:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIRC, passing as single layer view as a RENDER_ATTACHMENT is fine. The restriction is only applied as a TEXTURE_BINDING.\n\n[from the propose](https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/compatibility-mode.md#6-array-texture-views-used-in-bind-groups-must-consist-of-the-entire-array-that-is-basearraylayer-must-be-zero-and-arraylayercount-must-be-equal-to-the-size-of-the-texture-array) the restriction only applies to bind group bindings (TEXTURE_BINDINGS) not to attachments in a render pass.",
      "parentUuid": "f22b6286_f2760a03",
      "revId": "e1922a21f12283a41150c7cff3ab305c816ea113",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
